tax:D25 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:rights "Original formulation of this package, offered under the terms of the ontology (CC BY 4.0). It reproduces no text, title or structure of the works that informed it."@en ;
    dcterms:source "Own formulation of this package, written on 2026-10-13 under the Owner's decision of the same day to build an own semantic corpus from the works read, copying neither their text nor their structure. Informed by: the Owner's own works (the O4SDLC pack, the domain engineering files, the AI4SE material, the 2013 thesis, the UAISE draft); ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207:2026, ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148:2018, ISO/IEC/IEEE 24641:2023 and a preview of ISO/IEC 26550:2015, as read by the Owner under a licence the Owner confirmed on 2026-10-13; the IIBA BABOK Guide v3 (a member copy); SWEBOK Guide v4.0; the SEBoK; the NASA Systems Engineering Handbook; the SEI Framework for Software Product Line Practice."@en ;
    skos:inScheme tax:PracticeConceptCorpusScheme ;
    skos:notation "25" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Practice Concept Corpus (own formulation for the seven areas)"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Concepts for the seven areas that lack a public standard text (domain engineering, application engineering, business analysis, technical analysis, integration and build, transition and release, disposal), stated in this package's own words and grouped by the question each group answers, not by the chapters or clauses of any source. Each concept links, by skos:related, to the areas it serves. No sentence, heading, ordering, numbering or count of the informing works is reproduced; where a concept has a familiar name, the definition is this package's own and may differ from any source's. The corpus is a statement of this package's understanding, written with AI assistance, and has not been reviewed by a domain specialist."@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf tax:PracticeConceptCorpusScheme .

